IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sfp-dates`
IMPORT `sfp-claims`

-- Succession Act 2006 (NSW), Chapter 3 -- worked cases for every exported question in sfp-claims.l4.
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's output. Each
-- assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Dates and amounts are illustrative.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the calendar day`

`nc` MEANS `I am not their child`
`ch` MEANS `I am their child`
`posthumous` MEANS `I was born after they died, from a pregnancy that began before their death, and lived at least 30 days`
`of the relationship` MEANS `I was born of sexual relations between them and their de facto or domestic partner`
`adopted by both` MEANS `I was adopted by both them and their de facto or domestic partner`
`parental responsibility` MEANS `they and their de facto or domestic partner both had parental responsibility for my long-term welfare`
`father of the partner's child` MEANS `my mother was their de facto partner and they are, or are presumed to be, my father`
`two mothers` MEANS `they and their female de facto partner, both women, are presumed to be my parents`
`no rel` MEANS `they were in no de facto or domestic relationship`
`df` MEANS `they were in a de facto relationship`
`dom` MEANS `they were in a domestic relationship that was not a de facto relationship`

§§ `ss 3, 57 -- Am I an eligible person`

-- Arguments: commenced; married at death; de facto at death; how child; deceased in a de facto or domestic relationship
-- at death; former spouse; ever dependent; grandchild; household member; both adults; living together at death; care
-- given; for fee; on behalf of another.
-- s 57(1)(a) spouse.
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` TRUE TRUE FALSE `nc` `no rel` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Death before Chapter 3 commenced: the 1982 Act, outside the sources.
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` FALSE TRUE FALSE `nc` `no rel` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b) de facto partner.
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` TRUE FALSE TRUE `nc` `no rel` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (c) child; a posthumous child (s 3(2)).
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` TRUE FALSE FALSE `ch` `no rel` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` TRUE FALSE FALSE `posthumous` `no rel` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 57(2): heads count only if the deceased was in a de facto or domestic relationship at death.
-- s 57(2)(a), (b), (e) count for a domestic relationship too; (c), (d) need a de facto relationship.
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` TRUE FALSE FALSE `parental responsibility` `dom` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` TRUE FALSE FALSE `father of the partner's child` `df` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` TRUE FALSE FALSE `father of the partner's child` `dom` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` TRUE FALSE FALSE `two mothers` `df` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` TRUE FALSE FALSE `two mothers` `dom` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` TRUE FALSE FALSE `two mothers` `no rel` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` TRUE FALSE FALSE `parental responsibility` `df` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` TRUE FALSE FALSE `parental responsibility` `no rel` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` TRUE FALSE FALSE `adopted by both` `df` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` TRUE FALSE FALSE `of the relationship` `no rel` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (d) former spouse.
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` TRUE FALSE FALSE `nc` `no rel` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (e) dependent grandchild; dependent household member; dependent only; grandchild only.
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` TRUE FALSE FALSE `nc` `no rel` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` TRUE FALSE FALSE `nc` `no rel` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` TRUE FALSE FALSE `nc` `no rel` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` TRUE FALSE FALSE `nc` `no rel` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (f) close personal relationship (s 3(3), (4)).
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` TRUE FALSE FALSE `nc` `no rel` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` TRUE FALSE FALSE `nc` `no rel` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` TRUE FALSE FALSE `nc` `no rel` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` TRUE FALSE FALSE `nc` `no rel` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` TRUE FALSE FALSE `nc` `no rel` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` TRUE FALSE FALSE `nc` `no rel` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A spouse who also cared: eligible as a spouse (the close personal relationship excludes a marriage, not the spouse).
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` TRUE TRUE FALSE `nc` `no rel` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No head at all.
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` TRUE FALSE FALSE `nc` `no rel` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

