§§ `s 58 -- Can my application be made when I file it`

-- Arguments: day of death; day filed; Court's order for sufficient cause; parties' consent.
-- The last day, the day after, and the day of death.
#ASSERT `Can my application be made when I file it` (`d` 15 3 2024) (`d` 15 3 2025) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my application be made when I file it` (`d` 15 3 2024) (`d` 16 3 2025) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can my application be made when I file it` (`d` 15 3 2024) (`d` 14 3 2025) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my application be made when I file it` (`d` 15 3 2024) (`d` 15 3 2024) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Out of time, with the Court's order or the parties' consent.
#ASSERT `Can my application be made when I file it` (`d` 15 3 2024) (`d` 16 3 2025) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my application be made when I file it` (`d` 15 3 2024) (`d` 1 6 2027) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A death on 29 February: the last day is 28 February (fork F3).
#ASSERT `Can my application be made when I file it` (`d` 29 2 2024) (`d` 28 2 2025) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my application be made when I file it` (`d` 29 2 2024) (`d` 1 3 2025) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Filing dated before the death is not an application under s 58 (fork F4).
#ASSERT `Can my application be made when I file it` (`d` 15 3 2024) (`d` 14 3 2024) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 59 -- Can the Court make a family provision order for me`

-- A spouse at death (died 15 March 2024, no extension or consent), with the later facts as arguments: day filed;
-- release approved; factors warrant; adequate provision not made; earlier applications; substantial detrimental change;
-- property not revealed; estate substantially greater; would not have made the earlier order.
GIVEN `filed` IS A DATE, `released` IS A BOOLEAN, `factors` IS A BOOLEAN, `inadequate` IS A BOOLEAN, `earlier` IS A `My earlier applications for this estate`, `change` IS A BOOLEAN, `unrevealed` IS A BOOLEAN, `greater` IS A BOOLEAN, `would not` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`for a spouse` `filed` `released` `factors` `inadequate` `earlier` `change` `unrevealed` `greater` `would not` MEANS
    `Can the Court make a family provision order for me` TRUE TRUE FALSE `nc` `no rel` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 15 3 2024) `filed` FALSE FALSE `released` `factors` `inadequate` `earlier` `change` `unrevealed` `greater` `would not`

-- The same for a former spouse only.
GIVEN `filed` IS A DATE, `released` IS A BOOLEAN, `factors` IS A BOOLEAN, `inadequate` IS A BOOLEAN, `earlier` IS A `My earlier applications for this estate`, `change` IS A BOOLEAN, `unrevealed` IS A BOOLEAN, `greater` IS A BOOLEAN, `would not` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`for a former spouse` `filed` `released` `factors` `inadequate` `earlier` `change` `unrevealed` `greater` `would not` MEANS
    `Can the Court make a family provision order for me` TRUE FALSE FALSE `nc` `no rel` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 15 3 2024) `filed` FALSE FALSE `released` `factors` `inadequate` `earlier` `change` `unrevealed` `greater` `would not`

`none before` MEANS `I have not applied before`
`order before` MEANS `a family provision order was made for me before`
`refused before` MEANS `my earlier application was refused`

-- The ordinary case; the factors finding is not needed for a spouse.
#ASSERT `for a spouse` (`d` 1 9 2024) FALSE FALSE TRUE `none before` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 59(1)(c): adequate provision made.
#ASSERT `for a spouse` (`d` 1 9 2024) FALSE FALSE FALSE `none before` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 58(2): filed the day after the 12 months, no order or consent; filed on the last day.
#ASSERT `for a spouse` (`d` 16 3 2025) FALSE FALSE TRUE `none before` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `for a spouse` (`d` 15 3 2025) FALSE FALSE TRUE `none before` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 95(1): an approved release.
#ASSERT `for a spouse` (`d` 1 9 2024) TRUE FALSE TRUE `none before` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 59(1)(b): a former spouse needs the factors finding.
#ASSERT `for a former spouse` (`d` 1 9 2024) FALSE FALSE TRUE `none before` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `for a former spouse` (`d` 1 9 2024) FALSE TRUE TRUE `none before` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 59(3): a second order needs a detrimental change, or all three undisclosed-property conditions.
#ASSERT `for a spouse` (`d` 1 9 2024) FALSE FALSE TRUE `order before` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `for a spouse` (`d` 1 9 2024) FALSE FALSE TRUE `order before` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `for a spouse` (`d` 1 9 2024) FALSE FALSE TRUE `order before` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `for a spouse` (`d` 1 9 2024) FALSE FALSE TRUE `order before` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 59(4): after a refusal, only the undisclosed-property conditions; a detrimental change does not help.
#ASSERT `for a spouse` (`d` 1 9 2024) FALSE FALSE TRUE `refused before` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `for a spouse` (`d` 1 9 2024) FALSE FALSE TRUE `refused before` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Death before Chapter 3; not eligible; late but with consent.
#ASSERT `Can the Court make a family provision order for me` FALSE TRUE FALSE `nc` `no rel` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 15 3 2008) (`d` 1 9 2008) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `none before` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can the Court make a family provision order for me` TRUE FALSE FALSE `nc` `no rel` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 15 3 2024) (`d` 1 9 2024) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE `none before` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the Court make a family provision order for me` TRUE FALSE FALSE `ch` `no rel` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 15 3 2024) (`d` 1 9 2026) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE `none before` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

