§§ `ss 75, 76 -- Is this a relevant property transaction`

-- Arguments: what they did; full valuable consideration; property became held by another (for "some other act").
#ASSERT `Is this a relevant property transaction` `they gave away or transferred property during their life` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is this a relevant property transaction` `they gave away or transferred property during their life` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is this a relevant property transaction` `they did not sever a joint tenancy before they died` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is this a relevant property transaction` `they did not exercise a power to appoint or dispose of property outside their estate` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is this a relevant property transaction` `they did not exercise a power to extinguish another person's interest in their property` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is this a relevant property transaction` `they did not change the beneficiary of, or surrender or deal with, a life assurance policy on their life` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is this a relevant property transaction` `property passed to someone because of their membership of a superannuation or other fund, scheme or body` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is this a relevant property transaction` `property passed to someone because of their membership of a superannuation or other fund, scheme or body` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is this a relevant property transaction` `they entered into a contract disposing of property out of their estate` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is this a relevant property transaction` `they entered into a contract disposing of property out of their estate` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 75(3): a will, even with nothing given in return.
#ASSERT `Is this a relevant property transaction` `they made a will, or did not make one` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is this a relevant property transaction` `some other act or omission of theirs` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is this a relevant property transaction` `some other act or omission of theirs` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 79, 80, 83, 88-90 -- Can this property be designated as notional estate for me`

-- A transaction (no full consideration, property held by another) by a person who died on 10 June 2024, with a family
-- provision order to be made, an insufficient estate and a first application filed on 1 September 2024 (in time).
-- Arguments: what they did; the day it took effect; intent to deny or limit; moral obligation substantially greater;
-- disadvantage (s 83). Here the dead person's death ended any power, right to sever or membership (s 77(2), (3)).
GIVEN `what` IS A `What they did or did not do`, `effect` IS A DATE, `intent` IS A BOOLEAN, `moral` IS A BOOLEAN, `disadvantage` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`transaction case` `what` `effect` `intent` `moral` `disadvantage` MEANS
    `Can this property be designated as notional estate for me` `it went through a transaction they entered into` `what` FALSE TRUE FALSE `effect` (`d` 10 6 2024) `intent` `moral` `disadvantage` TRUE `the estate is not enough for the order the Court thinks should be made` (`d` 1 9 2024) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- The same, where an event other than the death ended the power, right to sever or membership; `effect` is that
-- event's day (s 77(2), (3)).
GIVEN `what` IS A `What they did or did not do`, `effect` IS A DATE, `intent` IS A BOOLEAN, `moral` IS A BOOLEAN, `disadvantage` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ended by another event case` `what` `effect` `intent` `moral` `disadvantage` MEANS
    `Can this property be designated as notional estate for me` `it went through a transaction they entered into` `what` FALSE TRUE TRUE `effect` (`d` 10 6 2024) `intent` `moral` `disadvantage` TRUE `the estate is not enough for the order the Court thinks should be made` (`d` 1 9 2024) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- A distribution from the estate (death 10 June 2024; the 12 months end on 10 June 2025), with the Division 3 facts as
-- arguments: order to be made; state of the estate; day filed; estate already had an order; trustee-only unvested
-- holding; other special circumstances; other property of a trustee.
GIVEN `fpo` IS A BOOLEAN, `state` IS A `The state of the estate`, `filed` IS A DATE, `had order` IS A BOOLEAN, `trustee only` IS A BOOLEAN, `special` IS A BOOLEAN, `other property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`distribution case` `fpo` `state` `filed` `had order` `trustee only` `special` `other property` MEANS
    `Can this property be designated as notional estate for me` `it was distributed from their estate` `they made a will, or did not make one` FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2025) (`d` 10 6 2024) FALSE FALSE FALSE `fpo` `state` `filed` `had order` `trustee only` `special` `other property`

`gift` MEANS `they gave away or transferred property during their life`
`not enough` MEANS `the estate is not enough for the order the Court thinks should be made`

-- s 80(2)(a): the first day of the three years, the day before it, and no intent.
#ASSERT `transaction case` `gift` (`d` 10 6 2021) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `transaction case` `gift` (`d` 9 6 2021) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `transaction case` `gift` (`d` 1 1 2023) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 80(2)(b): the first day of the one year, the day before it.
#ASSERT `transaction case` `gift` (`d` 10 6 2023) FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `transaction case` `gift` (`d` 9 6 2023) FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 80(2)(c) with s 77(2), (3): ended by the death, a joint tenancy or fund benefit takes effect on the death, whenever
-- it was set up.
#ASSERT `transaction case` `they did not sever a joint tenancy before they died` (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `transaction case` `property passed to someone because of their membership of a superannuation or other fund, scheme or body` (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 77(2), (3): ended by an event other than the death, ten years before it: outside every s 80(2) window.
#ASSERT `ended by another event case` `they did not exercise a power to appoint or dispose of property outside their estate` (`d` 10 6 2014) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `ended by another event case` `they did not change the beneficiary of, or surrender or deal with, a life assurance policy on their life` (`d` 10 6 2014) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `ended by another event case` `property passed to someone because of their membership of a superannuation or other fund, scheme or body` (`d` 10 6 2014) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Ended by another event within the windows: (a) with intent, first day and the day before; (b) with and without the
-- moral obligation.
#ASSERT `ended by another event case` `they did not exercise a power to extinguish another person's interest in their property` (`d` 10 6 2021) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `ended by another event case` `they did not exercise a power to extinguish another person's interest in their property` (`d` 9 6 2021) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `ended by another event case` `they did not sever a joint tenancy before they died` (`d` 10 6 2023) FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `ended by another event case` `they did not sever a joint tenancy before they died` (`d` 10 6 2023) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 83: no disadvantage found.
#ASSERT `transaction case` `they did not sever a joint tenancy before they died` (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 80(2)(c): a contract taking effect after the death; a gift taking effect on the day of death is in the windows, not (c) (fork F9).
#ASSERT `transaction case` `they entered into a contract disposing of property out of their estate` (`d` 11 6 2024) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `transaction case` `gift` (`d` 10 6 2024) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `transaction case` `gift` (`d` 10 6 2024) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not a relevant property transaction: a will.
#ASSERT `transaction case` `they made a will, or did not make one` (`d` 1 1 2024) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
