§§ `ss 81, 82 -- Can property passed on by the first recipient be designated as notional estate for me`

-- Arguments: how it passed on; power over the first recipient; their dealing was a relevant property transaction; power
-- arose only from a trustee holding; administration of their estate granted; special circumstances; disadvantage
-- (s 83); then the Division 3 facts (order to be made; state; day of death; day filed; estate already had an order;
-- trustee only; other special; other property). Death 10 June 2024, filed 1 September 2024 unless stated.
`passed on` MEANS `the first recipient passed it on through a transaction of their own`
`held by LR` MEANS `the first recipient has died and their legal representative holds it`
`distributed on` MEANS `the first recipient has died and it was distributed from their estate`

#ASSERT `Can property passed on by the first recipient be designated as notional estate for me` `passed on` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `not enough` (`d` 10 6 2024) (`d` 1 9 2024) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can property passed on by the first recipient be designated as notional estate for me` `passed on` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE `not enough` (`d` 10 6 2024) (`d` 1 9 2024) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can property passed on by the first recipient be designated as notional estate for me` `passed on` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `not enough` (`d` 10 6 2024) (`d` 1 9 2024) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can property passed on by the first recipient be designated as notional estate for me` `passed on` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `not enough` (`d` 10 6 2024) (`d` 1 9 2024) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can property passed on by the first recipient be designated as notional estate for me` `passed on` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE `not enough` (`d` 10 6 2024) (`d` 1 9 2024) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 82(2)(a): no special circumstances needed; administration needed; not a trustee-only power.
#ASSERT `Can property passed on by the first recipient be designated as notional estate for me` `held by LR` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE `not enough` (`d` 10 6 2024) (`d` 1 9 2024) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can property passed on by the first recipient be designated as notional estate for me` `held by LR` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE `not enough` (`d` 10 6 2024) (`d` 1 9 2024) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can property passed on by the first recipient be designated as notional estate for me` `held by LR` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE `not enough` (`d` 10 6 2024) (`d` 1 9 2024) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 82(2)(b): special circumstances needed.
#ASSERT `Can property passed on by the first recipient be designated as notional estate for me` `distributed on` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `not enough` (`d` 10 6 2024) (`d` 1 9 2024) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can property passed on by the first recipient be designated as notional estate for me` `distributed on` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE `not enough` (`d` 10 6 2024) (`d` 1 9 2024) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 90(1)(a): filed after the 12 months, with no trustee-only holding or special circumstances; with special circumstances.
#ASSERT `Can property passed on by the first recipient be designated as notional estate for me` `passed on` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `not enough` (`d` 10 6 2024) (`d` 11 6 2025) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can property passed on by the first recipient be designated as notional estate for me` `passed on` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `not enough` (`d` 10 6 2024) (`d` 11 6 2025) FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 88: the estate is enough.
#ASSERT `Can property passed on by the first recipient be designated as notional estate for me` `passed on` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `the estate is enough` (`d` 10 6 2024) (`d` 1 9 2024) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 89(2) -- What is the most that can be designated as notional estate`

-- Arguments: provision the Court thinks should be made; costs ordered from notional estate; what the estate can supply.
#ASSERT `What is the most that can be designated as notional estate` 100000 20000 50000 EQUALS 70000
#ASSERT `What is the most that can be designated as notional estate` 100000 0 100000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `What is the most that can be designated as notional estate` 100000 0 150000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `What is the most that can be designated as notional estate` 100000 5000 0 EQUALS 105000
#ASSERT `What is the most that can be designated as notional estate` 100000 0 99999 EQUALS 1

§§ `ss 93, 94 -- Is the legal representative protected if they distribute before my claim`

-- Death 1 January 2024: six months end 1 July 2024; twelve months 1 January 2025. Arguments: death; distribution;
-- notice of intended distribution given; day given; day specified; what I told them; properly made; my written consent
-- or no-claim notice; immediate needs of a dependent eligible person.
`no notice` MEANS `I have given the legal representative no written notice`
`intended` MEANS `I gave written signed notice of my application or intended application`
`commenced` MEANS `I gave written notice that my application has been commenced in the Court, or served a copy of it`

-- s 93: all conditions met; a 29-day notice period; distribution on the specified day and the day after.
#ASSERT `Is the legal representative protected if they distribute before my claim` (`d` 1 1 2024) (`d` 2 8 2024) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2024) (`d` 1 7 2024) `no notice` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the legal representative protected if they distribute before my claim` (`d` 1 1 2024) (`d` 2 8 2024) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2024) (`d` 30 6 2024) `no notice` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the legal representative protected if they distribute before my claim` (`d` 1 1 2024) (`d` 1 8 2024) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2024) (`d` 1 8 2024) `no notice` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the legal representative protected if they distribute before my claim` (`d` 1 1 2024) (`d` 2 8 2024) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2024) (`d` 1 8 2024) `no notice` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 93(1)(a): exactly six months after the death, and the day before.
#ASSERT `Is the legal representative protected if they distribute before my claim` (`d` 1 1 2024) (`d` 1 7 2024) TRUE (`d` 1 5 2024) (`d` 1 6 2024) `no notice` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the legal representative protected if they distribute before my claim` (`d` 1 1 2024) (`d` 30 6 2024) TRUE (`d` 1 5 2024) (`d` 1 6 2024) `no notice` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No notice of intended distribution; not properly made.
#ASSERT `Is the legal representative protected if they distribute before my claim` (`d` 1 1 2024) (`d` 2 8 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 6 2024) (`d` 1 7 2024) `no notice` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the legal representative protected if they distribute before my claim` (`d` 1 1 2024) (`d` 2 8 2024) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2024) (`d` 1 7 2024) `no notice` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 94(4), (5): my notice of an intended application; before and on the twelve months; commenced or served.
#ASSERT `Is the legal representative protected if they distribute before my claim` (`d` 1 1 2024) (`d` 2 8 2024) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2024) (`d` 1 7 2024) `intended` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the legal representative protected if they distribute before my claim` (`d` 1 1 2024) (`d` 31 12 2024) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2024) (`d` 1 7 2024) `intended` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the legal representative protected if they distribute before my claim` (`d` 1 1 2024) (`d` 1 1 2025) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2024) (`d` 1 7 2024) `intended` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the legal representative protected if they distribute before my claim` (`d` 1 1 2024) (`d` 1 1 2025) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2024) (`d` 1 7 2024) `intended` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the legal representative protected if they distribute before my claim` (`d` 1 1 2024) (`d` 1 2 2025) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2024) (`d` 1 7 2024) `commenced` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 94(1), (2): immediate needs of a dependant, even with my application commenced; s 94(3): my written consent.
#ASSERT `Is the legal representative protected if they distribute before my claim` (`d` 1 1 2024) (`d` 1 2 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2024) (`d` 1 1 2024) `commenced` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the legal representative protected if they distribute before my claim` (`d` 1 1 2024) (`d` 1 2 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2024) (`d` 1 1 2024) `no notice` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the legal representative protected if they distribute before my claim` (`d` 1 1 2024) (`d` 1 2 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2024) (`d` 1 1 2024) `no notice` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

